<.shell title="Call and text" current={:call_and_text}>
  <h1>Call and text</h1>
  <p class="lead">Call and Text buttons by a phone number.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Phone</dt>
      <dd>
        604-555-1234
        <.call_and_text
          id="call-and-text-demo"
          phone="6045551234"
          touch_only={false}
          class="mt-2"
        />
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    By a member's phone number where someone may want to reach them now: the member's details, yet to arrive, and no-shows.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A number shown to check or match, such as in a pasted attendance report. Show the number alone.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.call_and_text id="…" phone=&#123;member.phone&#125; /&gt;</code>
    under the number, shown with <code>Phone.format/1</code>. It shows only on a touch screen, because a desktop often has no app for
    <code>tel:</code>
    and <code>sms:</code>
    links. The example above shows it everywhere with <code>touch_only=&#123;false&#125;</code>. With no number it shows nothing.
  </p>
</.shell>
